== playbook entries (explain-error.sh on each distinct ERROR/WARN/panic line)
  dlq-missing-relation         6  a table EP reads does not exist in the database it is connected to
  dlq-cached-plan              2  SQLSTATE 0A000: a Rails migration changed a table that EP reads with SELECT * (pgx statement cache) -> retryable failure
  dlq-build-enriched-event     1  event timestamp unparsable or of an unsupported type -> DLQ (non-retryable)
  dlq-bm-not-found             1  no billable metric for (organization_id, code) -> DLQ (non-retryable, not sent to Sentry)
  dlq-evaluate-expression      1  lago-expression returned nil for the metric's custom expression -> DLQ (non-retryable)
  dlq-fetch-subscription       1  subscription lookup failed with a DB/badger error (not "not found": a missing subscription is NOT an error, the event is enriched with subscription_id "") -> retryable
  dlq-pay-in-advance           1  charges lookup failed after the enriched event was ALREADY produced -> retryable; a redelivery duplicates the enriched event
  dlq-flag-refresh             1  ZADD to the Redis ZSET subscription_refreshed_v2 failed -> retryable (enriched already produced)
  dlq-empty-code               1  produce to events_enriched / events_charged_in_advance failed -> DLQ row with error_code "" and the record is COMMITTED (no per-event ERROR line)
  loss-unmarshal               1  raw record is not valid JSON for models.Event: committed, NO DLQ, Sentry only = LOST
  loss-retryable-skip          1  the FIRST record of a batch failed retryably, so nothing was committed; if any later batch on that partition commits, the failed offset is skipped forever (no DLQ, no retry)
  run-unknown-topic            1  a topic EP produces to (or consumes) does not exist on the cluster
  run-redis-pool               1  go-redis cannot open a connection (plain-text line from go-redis, not JSON)
